      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s community museum, housed in the historic former Bank of Coleridge building, showcases artifacts from the 1840s to today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.heartofnorthcarolina.com/cities-and-towns/ramseur/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Parts of the 1968 film Killers Three were shot in Ramseur, with many locals appearing as extras.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ramseur%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ramseur Lake, a Pell Water Recreation Facility, offers picnic shelters, a playground, fishing piers, and limits motorboats to 10 horsepower.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.heartofnorthcarolina.com/cities-and-towns/ramseur/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Millstone Creek Orchards lets visitors pick apples, peaches, berries, grapes, and pumpkins, and the nearby Apple Barn Country Store serves famous cider slushies.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
